A set name (dep) equal to an import qualifier that appears in BOTH the file being
overwritten (a_gen.go, which sorts lexically first) AND a hand-written sibling
(server.go). plumb records the sibling's base rather than the output file's (the
output file's imports are plumb's to rewrite, but the sibling's are not), so the
collision is reported instead of silently emitted (Go forbids one identifier being
both a file-block import name and the package-block func).
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: a_gen.go
error-is: ErrSetNameCollision
-- example.com/dep/dep.go --
package dep

var Marker = 0
-- example.com/app/a_gen.go --
package app

import "example.com/dep"

var _ = dep.Marker
-- example.com/app/server.go --
package app

import "example.com/dep"

var Client = dep.Marker
-- example.com/app/providers.go --
package app

type Thing struct{}

//plumb:dep
func MakeThing() *Thing { return &Thing{} }
